  "summary_md": "IT services firms are undergoing a sweeping AI-driven repositioning, creating stark divergence across the batch. On the positive side, WYY extended a multi-year streak of profitability fueled by FedRAMP-certified federal demand, IBEX raised full-year guidance behind double-digit organic growth and an AI partnership, and TSSI lifted its outlook on hyperscale AI rack integration orders. In contrast, VEEA remains pre-revenue with heavy dilutive financing, and SLAI’s rapid crypto-to-AI pivot is clouded by an NYSE listing notice. The most dramatic strategic moves come from DTST, which sold its legacy cloud unit, shrank its share count by ~72%, and went all-in on sovereign AI continuity, and SHAZ, whose landmark multi-year cloud AI contract ignited extreme stock volatility. A common thread is the reliance on convertible notes and equity lines (SHAZ, WYFI, DAIC) to fund these transformations, while a wave of divestitures, acquisitions, and rebrandings (CNDT, CYCU, TTGT) underscores an industry actively reshaping its portfolio.",
  "summary_date": "2026-05-28"
